{"c":[{"id":"4d23ece8fc1b906f","sum":"Chrome titles its top AXGroup/AXWebArea (keep out of keys), rejects AXManualAccessibility yet exposes web AX; background fixtures need makeKey(); caret-screen acts only in --act-pids. Fill recency: window before the form's last focus. Use RollingText.findAll; 250 ms tick grid.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"0f5b9811057334dd","sum":"Reader AX lore: Chrome titles its top AXGroup/AXWebArea (keep out of keys), rejects AXManualAccessibility yet exposes web AX, posts no DOM-text notices (E1/E8); background AppKit fixtures need makeKey() for focus; caret-screen acts only in --act-pids, rechecks fail closed.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b99fccd1ca3e2300","sum":"Chrome: top AXGroup is named after the window title and AXWebArea after the page title, so keep both out of element keys (E8); Chrome/Helium reject AXManualAccessibility (-25205) yet expose web AX, Electron accepts it; web pages post no AX notification for DOM text changes (E1).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T100848Z-2317db88abe7ef57","text":"Chrome names its top AXGroup after the window title and AXWebArea after the page title; keep both out of element keys or every key moves on a title change (E8).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T100848Z-7a26e801e62c7446","text":"Chrome and Helium reject AXManualAccessibility (-25205) but still expose web AX; Electron apps accept it. Web pages post no AX notification for DOM text, insert or remove changes (E1).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7284de3ea53779af","sum":"Fixtures and acting: a non-frontmost AppKit app posts AX focus only inside its key window (fixtures makeKey() before makeFirstResponder); caret-screen write/press act only in --act-pids, a subset of --only-pids, and rechecks fail closed on unreadable role/subrole/value/label.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T100848Z-bac1844f3b887c52","text":"A non-frontmost AppKit app posts AX focus notifications only inside its key window; fixtures call makeKey() (no activation) before makeFirstResponder.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T114801Z-32531afb7e4fe1e0","text":"caret-screen write/press verbs act only in --act-pids, which must be a subset of --only-pids; without it the reader only reads. Rechecks fail closed on unreadable role/subrole/value/label.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"cfe456d6c1deaf07","sum":"Fill recency is the window before the form's last focus (the latest made Jev answer none); caret-fixture deactivates on becoming active, so poll lsappinfo front in GUI runs. RollingText.find credits the latest window: use findAll. Replay tests tick on a fixed 250 ms stream grid.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"55197345bf228f3c","sum":"Fill recency takes the window before the form's last focus (the latest focus made Jev answer none); caret-fixture spawned from the frontmost app held the foreground, so it now deactivates on becoming active; poll lsappinfo front in GUI runs.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T114801Z-431742a743596ba6","text":"Fill recency: take the just-left window from focus history (the window before the form's last focus), not the latest focus; latest-focus made Jev answer none on most fields once the user moved to another form.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T130715Z-7922f91e68f9ff52","text":"caret-fixture spawned from the frontmost app (T3 or a terminal) became the active app and held the foreground for a whole run; it now deactivates on becoming active. Poll lsappinfo front during GUI runs.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"478a07b8a88c6346","sum":"Pattern code: RollingText.find credits a value seen in two windows to the most recent one; use findAll and pick the window that explains every round. Replay tests tick the helper on a fixed 250 ms grid of stream time like main.ts, or dense streams delay every transfer.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T143157Z-06f3c5b5c6254f49","text":"A value shown in two windows is credited by RollingText.find to the most recently seen one; pattern code must use findAll and pick the window that explains every round, or loop columns look like different sources.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T143157Z-9c4a82917dc22e00","text":"Replaying reader streams in tests: tick helper on a fixed 250 ms grid of stream time like main.ts; ticking only inside gaps >250 ms delays every transfer when messages are dense.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"648367d653fa1e3a","sum":"Gate path: no SQLite writes, flush on tick. Keep the pending watch's trailing debounce. No execFileSync in eval polls. Background fixture: stdin focus moves AX focus. Human input: powerd UserIsActive (B5). Count a departure once. Shadow store: ro .backup. Markers: structure.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c3649964eaa98e3b","sum":"No SQLite writes on the gate's event path (buffer, flush on tick). Pending watch: status text and a vanishing progress bar arrive in separate snapshots; keep the trailing debounce. Background-only fixture: stdin 'focus NAME' still moves AX focus. No execFileSync in eval polls.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"e6572ec977c106ea","sum":"No SQLite writes on the pattern gate's event path (one insert stalled 11 ms at load 15-69); buffer and flush on tick. A --background-only caret-fixture reports no key window, yet stdin 'focus NAME' still moves AX focus; the reader sees leave and focus walks.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T143157Z-fc39a0364b9ecb3f","text":"Pattern gate runs on the event path: no SQLite writes there (one decision-log insert stalled 11 ms at load 15-69); decisions are buffered and flushed on tick.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T160236Z-60fc41a933501ea6","text":"A --background-only (prohibited) caret-fixture reports no key window, yet stdin 'focus NAME' (makeKey + makeFirstResponder) still moves AX focus; the reader sees leave and focus walks.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e21a3ad8c4a3fa82","sum":"Pending watch: a finished job's status text and vanishing progress bar arrive in separate snapshots; keep the trailing debounce or Jev judges a half-changed window. Eval scripts: no execFileSync in polling loops (lsappinfo every 100 ms added 150-250 ms to latencies, B4).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T160237Z-6009f034277d69a2","text":"Pending watch: a finished job's status text and its vanishing progress bar arrive in separate snapshots; without the trailing debounce the first Jev answer is about a half-changed window and is stale.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T160237Z-ba6e47628dfc0d66","text":"Eval scripts: never execFileSync in a polling loop. lsappinfo every 100 ms held the in-process helper's event loop and added 150-250 ms to every measured latency (B4).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"33f4ffb90faaf6ab","sum":"Hardware input shows only as powerd's UserIsActive in pmset -g log (B5). One window departure reaches the helper up to 3 times; count it once. Read the shadow store via sqlite3 mode=ro .backup only. Pending markers come from structure, not a sidebar 'Working' text (B6).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"6aeaadf7a5a96e75","sum":"Hardware input shows only as powerd's UserIsActive in pmset -g log (B5). The helper sees one window departure up to 3 times (appSwitch, leave walk, focus elsewhere): count per departure; a return is a focused walk of a departed window.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T173801Z-d9e0d3a584c9d36e","text":"Human activity on this Mac: only powerd's UserIsActive 'kernel.useractive' in pmset -g log marks hardware input; agents' posted events raise WindowServer per-process assertions, and WindowServer per-device ones stay raised for days (B5).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T173802Z-3bfd0ad97555af7b","text":"Helper reports one window departure up to three times (appSwitch, leave walk, focus elsewhere); count per departure, and detect a return as a focused walk of a departed window, since focusedWindowId does not change across an unreadable app.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7e4af4b925d02c75","sum":"Read the shadow store only via sqlite3 'file:...?mode=ro' .backup to a temp copy (opening it as Store writes a salt). Agent sidebars (T3, Codex) keep a 'Working' status for a thread's life: pending markers come from structure, not status words (B6).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T173802Z-57d66219a60e6cdb","text":"Read the shadow store only through sqlite3 'file:...?mode=ro' .backup into a temp copy; opening a data dir as Store creates a salt file and chmods it.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T201044Z-85ef58a913b9161a","text":"T3 Code and Codex list other agent threads in a left sidebar, each a button holding a status text ('Working') that lasts the thread's life; pending markers must come from structure (enabled stop button by the composer), not status words (B6 census).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
